<speak>It is surprisingly common for papers to be organised by memory rather than by labels. The difficulty appears when someone else moves them, even with the best intentions. A folder gives the household a shared place without requiring anyone to read what is inside. You could tell the family that loose personal correspondence belongs there, unopened, and leave the rest of the routine to yourself. On the bank side, if a document is difficult to locate in the digital inbox, we can help you find the relevant section. You do not need to ask a family member to search through your personal correspondence for you.</speak>